Z||000000||Darren's 87 coupe||10-15-2001||09:19 AM||||ok I am finally going to get to take the tarp off and start working on my 87 blue coupe now.  I have to haul it down from Tulsa this week and our move to OKC will be complete.  I was given this car several months ago and it has been in storage for 2 years.  The body is real nice and the interior is very very clean and all stock.  The engine on the other hand sucks.  It is a 4cyl with a 5 speed.  175,000miles.  It is leaking oil into the radiator and when i put a battery in it the other day it is cranking over but won't start unless i spray cold start into it.  then it burns that off and dies.  What am I looking at here?  Thanks for any help.<BR>Darren<P>P.s.  It was running when it got stored, but it did have the oil in the radiator at that time.||||reg||9
Z||000001||sdelgado||10-15-2001||11:34 AM||||I'm by no means an expert, but it could be the fuel pump.  Do you hear the fuel pump come on when you turn the ignition?  Check fuse for fuel pump too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Darren's 87 coupe||10-15-2001||11:47 AM||||yes i do hear it come on when i turn the key.  And i did put some fresh gas in it before i turned it over||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||10-15-2001||01:30 PM||||Check all ignition components.  Make sure all the spark plug wires are properly connected at the coils and the plugs.  Check all the wiring harnesses to see if mice have chewed through them while in storage.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||sdelgado||10-15-2001||04:39 PM||||Is the injector spraying?<P>I had a similar situation where my 86 2m4 sat for a long time and it would turn but not start.  replaced the fuel pump and it started right up. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||samoht||10-15-2001||04:47 PM||||well i think you have spark.. since starting fluid is alot more flammible it could be spark is not enough to ignite the gas.. first think to do is check your spark.. its been sitting 2 years i would go ahead and buy wires plugs cap and button for it.  check for fuel pressure at fuel rail..  if you have good spark and injectors are firing. play with the timing alittle..  Good luck. it can only be not enough of one and/or two things<P>85gt32||||reg||1
Z||000006||Darren's 87 coupe||10-15-2001||08:02 PM||||thanks guys this is really helpful, I'm going up tomorrow and I'll check it all out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||85 gt fiero||10-15-2001||08:24 PM||||also check youre fuel filter it could be clogged, and also there is a fuel cylinode {on the 84's} anyway but that could be bad the throttle body injector(tbi).Randy <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
